  "literature_notes": "All five ledger lines support tags at intracellular positions only. L1 and L2 place MBP/Twin-StrepII+mCherry at the N-terminus (residues 1\u2013350, intracellular). L3 and L4 place GFP at the C-terminus (residues 645\u2013793, intracellular), with L4 providing functional validation by whole-cell patch-clamp. L5 describes 'HA-TRPC1-F562A': the conventional 'HA-PROTEIN' naming indicates an N-terminal HA tag (intracellular); F562A is the dominant-negative point mutation in EC4 (residue 562 = Y in canonical numbering, within the extracellular span 559\u2013623), not the tag insertion site; the clip names no residue for the HA junction and cannot be pinned to an extracellular loop. TRPC1 has no extracellular terminus (both N- and C-termini are cytoplasmic), and no ledger line reports a tag inserted into any of the four extracellular loops (EC1: 361, 1 aa; EC2: 405\u2013422, 18 aa; EC3: 476\u2013496, 21 aa; EC4: 559\u2013623, 65 aa). Zero extracellular tag sites are supported.",
